`@web/site` builds static links at compile time. Import it explicitly in a
`.moth` file to use the site root and add site-relative paths.

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    @web/site

    home #= site.root
    guide #= [site.url:docs/getting-started/]
    #[:home=[home] guide=[guide]]
]

Don't start the suffix with `/`. The root follows the project's configured
`origin`, so the guide renders under `/moth/docs/getting-started/` when the
origin is `/moth`.

Unlike `site.url`, @../page (@web/page)'s `page.url()` reads the live browser
address at runtime. For the package contract see @#site (@web/site advanced).
